WEBVTT

00:00:00.910 --> 00:00:02.900
Friday, three coaches called.

00:00:03.070 --> 00:00:04.970
Kick's run said no errors.

00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:06.660
The table was still wrong.

00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:11.180
So Riley rewound, and asked first what should exist.

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:14.482
Eight schools, each hosting the other seven.

00:00:14.502 --> 00:00:19.500
Fifty-six matches. Two still to play, so fifty-four finished.

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:22.150
Then, what happened to each one.

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:24.240
Seven schedule pages saved.

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:26.560
Dunmore's never answered.

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:30.720
So its seven home matches came from the visitors' pages.

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:33.960
One match is final, with no score anywhere.

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:37.030
Cedar Grove and St. Lambert, September twenty-first.

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:39.720
Not nil-nil. Unknown.

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:43.810
Monday's message said fifty-three of fifty-four,

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:46.060
and named the one it was missing.

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:50.560
So here is the lesson. No errors describes the program.

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:53.910
Only a coverage record, written against what should exist,

00:00:53.930 --> 00:00:57.040
describes the data. And anything it can't see,

00:00:57.130 --> 00:01:00.080
it calls unknown. Never zero.

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:05.540
Tuesday. Kick adds a tidy rule.

00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:08.500
An S-T in a name means State.

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:10.900
The table now lists State Lambert.

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:14.530
St. Lambert (voicemail): Hi, this is St. Lambert soccer.

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:20.140
Saint, as in the saint. Your table says State Lambert.

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:22.220
We are not a state school.

00:01:22.550 --> 00:01:23.820
Please fix it.

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:27.230
Kick: Fixed. Saint stays Saint.

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:28.360
One line.

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:30.540
The code is fixed in a minute.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:34.810
Friday's table isn't. Ask the eight sites again and you get Tuesday's

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:38.620
pages, not Friday's. Dunmore's might not answer at all.

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:41.980
So Riley asks Kick one more thing.

00:01:42.670 --> 00:01:45.490
Riley: Can you rebuild Friday's table from the pages you kept,

00:01:45.510 --> 00:01:49.180
without asking a single site again, and show me you did?

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:55.700
Module 2: The raw archive
